# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local configuration
#
# .env holds DATABASE_URL and SUPPRESSION_HMAC_SALT. The salt is effectively
# write-once: rotating it orphans every existing Suppression row, which is how a
# person who asked never to be contacted again gets contacted again (A10). It must
# never reach a remote.
#
# The key-encryption key is NOT in any file — it lives in the macOS Keychain, and
# only ciphertext reaches Postgres (A5).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*-credentials.json
client_secret*.json
token.json
.secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
#
# generated/ is the Prisma client, produced by `npm run db:generate`. It is
# regenerated from schema.prisma on every clone, so committing it only creates
# merge conflicts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
generated/
dist/
build/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Next.js arrives at F3. next-env.d.ts is regenerated by `next build`; it is also
# deliberately excluded from tsconfig.backend.json, because that config's "*.ts"
# include pattern matches it and pulling it in re-types globalThis and process.env
# for the backend.
.next/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test, coverage and tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
.vitest/
.vite/
.eslintcache
.cache/
.turbo/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and runtime scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
pids/
*.pid
*.seed
tmp/
temp/
scratch/

# Local Postgres dumps and fixtures captured from live sources
*.dump
*.sql.gz
prisma/*.db
prisma/*.db-journal

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# VS Code: keep shared project settings, drop personal ones
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / assistant local state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.aider*
.md/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Markdown files
#
# The blanket `*.md` rule is here to keep assistant scratch notes out of the repo.
# As written through F0-F2 it also excluded `docs/` — which is every document this
# project depends on to be reconstructible:
#
#   docs/architecture-plan.md    the implementation contract, kept VERBATIM so it
#                                stays auditable. Every milestone is told never to
#                                edit it; none of them could have committed it.
#   docs/F*-HANDOVER.md          the whole deviation chain, 39 recorded decisions
#                                with their reasoning.
#   docs/handoff-llm-gateway.md  the LLM design spec.
#
# `handover.md` survived only because it was tracked before the rule existed. The
# rest were one `rm -rf` from being unrecoverable. Found in F3.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
!README.md
!handover.md
!docs/**/*.md
